diff --git a/PLANNING_AUTHORITY_INTEGRATION.md b/PLANNING_AUTHORITY_INTEGRATION.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..68ff9a8
--- /dev/null
+++ b/PLANNING_AUTHORITY_INTEGRATION.md
@@ -0,0 +1,28 @@
+# Planning authority geometry integration
+
+The Planning Data API and extracted planning-plan geometry are separate evidence classes.
+
+## Automatic Planning Data API use
+
+`--planning-data` queries bounded Planning Data entities. Exact feature datasets such as `listed-building-outline` can fill missing buildings or replace a conflicting OpenStreetMap outline through the gated planning-authority policy. Planning application geometry is treated as a red-line/site boundary only. It is retained for evidence and never interpreted as the approved building or path layout.
+
+## Extracted planning drawings
+
+Use `--planning-geometry FILE` for GeoJSON traced or extracted from a planning drawing, site plan, completion drawing, or as-built plan. Every collection must record its provider, source URL, and reuse licence. Every feature must record:
+
+- `kind`
+- `planning_geometry_role`
+- `planning_status`
+- `planning_confidence`
+- `planning_reference`
+- whether the proposal is implemented
+
+Automatic replacement is designed for `as-built`, `implemented-layout`, and current authoritative feature geometry. Pending, refused, withdrawn, expired, draft, weak, or ambiguous observations remain evidence-only.
+
+## Override modes
+
+- `off`: planning evidence can fill a clear gap but cannot replace OSM.
+- `gated`: default. Replacement requires implemented/current evidence, sufficient confidence, a unique matching OSM target, and enough geometric overlap or a same-name proximity match.
+- `authoritative`: also permits approved/granted evidence when explicitly selected. This can show an approved future layout before construction and should not be used for an as-built recreation unless that is intentional.
+
+The build writes `planning-authority-decisions.json`, recording every gap fill, corroboration, OSM replacement, rejected status, confidence rejection, and ambiguous conflict.
diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index beb9411..2628d60 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -465,3 +465,7 @@ node src/cli.mjs build \
 Generic public services can be declared with `--source-config`. Supported types are `ogc-api-features`, `arcgis-feature-layer`, `geojson-url`, and `geojson-file`. See `examples/supplemental-source-config.json`. Every configured source must declare its provider and licence. All configured vector services and files must return or contain WGS84 longitude/latitude geometry (`EPSG:4326`); reproject national-grid data before ingestion.
 
 The build writes `supplemental-sources.json`, containing request bounds, pages, cache state, accepted feature counts, failures, warnings, imagery candidates, and photo evidence. Optional service failures are recorded and skipped by default; add `--strict-supplemental-sources` when a source is mandatory.
+
+## Planning authority geometry
+
+Planning Data can now fill missing authoritative outlines and, under strict confidence/status/overlap gates, replace inaccurate OpenStreetMap geometry. Planning application site boundaries remain evidence-only because a red-line application boundary is not the approved physical layout. Extracted or traced implemented plans can be supplied with `--planning-geometry`; see `PLANNING_AUTHORITY_INTEGRATION.md` and `examples/planning-authority-geometry.geojson`.
